 "query": "Which instruments measure dissolved oxygen?",
 "answer": "The retrieved evidence supports four dissolved-oxygen instrument names in the RCA scope, with Oregon Slope Base Shallow Profiler Dissolved Oxygen appearing in multiple records [1, 4, 6]. I can identify the following from the evidence, but the set is not proven exhaustive.\n\nMatched instruments\n\n- Axial Seamount Shallow Profiler Dissolved Oxygen: a dissolved_oxygen sensor measuring seawater oxygen content at Axial Seamount Profiler; OOI site RS03AXPS / node PC03A; latitude 45.9316, longitude -129.9808, depth 2607 m; data available from 2015-04-01; units μmol/L; sample rate 1 Hz [2].\n\n- Oregon Slope Base Shallow Profiler Dissolved Oxygen:\n  - Catalogued RCA instance with canonical identifier RS01SBPS-PC01A-4A-DOSTAD103 [1].\n  - OOI API record at Oregon Slope Base / RS01SBPS, node PC01A; latitude 44.5101, longitude -125.3899, depth 2895 m; data available from 2015-04-01; units μmol/L; sample rate 1 Hz [4].\n  - Another OOI API record with the same name at Oregon Slope Base / RS01SBPS, node SF01A; described as a fast-response dissolved oxygen sensor on profiler; latitude 44.5101, longitude -125.3899, depth 2895 m; data available from 2015-04-01; units μmol/L; sample rate 1 Hz [6].\n\n- Oregon Slope Base Seafloor Dissolved Oxygen: catalogued RCA instance with canonical identifier RS01SLBS-LJ01A-12-DOSTAD101 at Oregon Slope Base Seafloor [3].\n\n- Oregon Slope Base Deep Profiler Dissolved Oxygen: a dissolved_oxygen sensor at Oregon Slope Base / RS01SBPD, node DP01A; latitude 44.5101, longitude -125.3899, depth 2906 m; data available from 2015-04-01; units μmol/L; sample rate 1 Hz [5].\n\nWhat the evidence does not establish\n\n- It does not establish a complete inventory of all dissolved-oxygen instruments in the full RCA Atlas/COSZO scope; it only supports the records retrieved here.\n- For the catalogued instances, the evidence does not separately enumerate sensor components [1, 3].",
